# Spring Boot CRUD API

A Spring Boot REST API demonstrating CRUD operations for employees using a custom DAO implementation with JPA EntityManager.

## Overview

This project is part of my Spring Boot learning journey.

The project demonstrates how to build a RESTful CRUD API using a layered architecture and JPA EntityManager for database operations.

## Architecture

The application follows a layered architecture:

```text
REST Controller
      ↓
Service Layer
      ↓
DAO Interface
      ↓
DAO Implementation
      ↓
JPA EntityManager
      ↓
MySQL Database
```

## Features

* Get all employees
* Get an employee by ID
* Create a new employee
* Update an employee
* Delete an employee
* Partial update using HTTP PATCH
* JSON request and response handling
* JPA EntityManager
* Custom DAO pattern
* Service layer
* REST Controller

## Technologies

* Java
* Spring Boot
* Spring Web
* Spring Data JPA / Jakarta Persistence
* JPA EntityManager
* MySQL
* Maven
* IntelliJ IDEA

## REST Endpoints

### Get All Employees

```http
GET /api/employees
```

Returns a list of all employees.

### Get Employee by ID

```http
GET /api/employees/{employeeId}
```

Returns an employee using the provided ID.

Example:

```http
GET /api/employees/1
```

### Create Employee

```http
POST /api/employees
```

Example request body:

```json
{
    "firstName": "Ahmed",
    "lastName": "Sabra",
    "email": "ahmed@example.com"
}
```

### Update Employee

```http
PUT /api/employees
```

Example request body:

```json
{
    "id": 1,
    "firstName": "Ahmed",
    "lastName": "Sabra",
    "email": "new@email.com"
}
```

### Delete Employee

```http
DELETE /api/employees/{employeeId}
```

Example:

```http
DELETE /api/employees/1
```

### Partial Update

```http
PATCH /api/employees/{employeeId}
```

Allows updating specific fields without sending the complete Employee object.

Example:

```json
{
    "email": "updated@email.com"
}
```

## Project Structure

```text
src/main/java/com/sabra/springboot/cruddemo
│
├── rest
│   └── EmployeeRestController
│
├── service
│   ├── EmployeeService
│   └── EmployeeServiceImpl
│
├── dao
│   ├── EmployeeDAO
│   └── EmployeeDAOJpaImpl
│
└── entity
    └── Employee
```

## What I Learned

Through this project, I practiced:

* Building REST APIs with Spring Boot
* Understanding HTTP methods such as GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, and DELETE
* Using `@RestController`
* Using `@RequestMapping`
* Using `@GetMapping`, `@PostMapping`, `@PutMapping`, `@PatchMapping`, and `@DeleteMapping`
* Using `@PathVariable`
* Using `@RequestBody`
* Converting JSON requests into Java objects
* Returning Java objects as JSON responses
* Creating POJO/Entity classes
* Using JPA EntityManager
* Creating a custom DAO layer
* Applying the Service Layer pattern
* Implementing CRUD database operations
* Implementing partial updates using Jackson `JsonMapper`

## Future Improvements

The project will be improved gradually as I continue learning Spring Boot.

Planned improvements include:

* Replacing the custom DAO implementation with Spring Data JPA `JpaRepository`
* Improving exception handling
* Adding global exception handling using `@ControllerAdvice`
* Adding validation
* Adding Spring Security and authentication/authorization
* Improving API responses and HTTP status handling
